WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.980
<b>Empire</b>

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.980
Emperor Wolfgang.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:38.030
Prince Shareef of the Land of Sand
 has sent you a gift.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.990
What would you like to do?

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.920
From the Land of Sand?

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.250
We've never had any involvement 
with them before.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.330
Bring it here.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.190
At once.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.990
It appears to be ordinary tableware.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.780
What does he say?

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.390
It seems he wishes to establish 
an alliance with our Empire.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.960
He says he sends this treasure from 
his nation as a token of friendship.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.890
This is a treasure?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:11.150
It is a magical vessel for 
chilling kaffa, he says.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:16.610
I see... I had heard that the Land of Sand
 was researching some unique magic.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.850
Shall we try it?

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.610
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.980
Do not blindly trust what 
is written. Use caution.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.240
I have brought the kaffa.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.550
Let's begin.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.300
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.450
Taste it.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.230
I-It's cold now!

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.040
You're right!

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.760
Your Majesty, it really is cold!

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.470
And there are no signs of any poisons!

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.360
Indeed, it is as cold as ice...

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.430
And delicious!

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.940
The Land of Sand and Prince Shareef...

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.190
I wish to see them with my own eyes now.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.410
Why are you sighing so?

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.410
Father!

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:48.050
When did you return?

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:51.660
Just now. I must leave again soon, however.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.540
I'm sorry to stop in so briefly, 
but I wanted to see your face.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.470
Thank you!

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.090
Father, where will you be going next?

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.880
The Land of Sand.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.050
The Land of Sand?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:09.730
Yes. It is a hot place, 
and the road there is long.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:13.090
But there is something I must 
find out once and for all.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.910
What's the matter? 
Your face is a bit flushed.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:20.500
You don't have a fever, do you?

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.820
Ah, no...

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.900
It's nothing. I'm just fine.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.400
I see. Very well, then.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.890
I'm glad I was able to see 
you in such good health.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.880
Well, I suppose it's time for me to go.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.020
Okay. Have a good trip, Father.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.200
Please be careful in your travels.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.490
So this is the Land of Sand?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.920
It's more lively than I expected.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.360
I had thought it was a nation that suffered 
from an inhospitable environment,

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.180
but it seems I was mistaken.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.100
Your Majesty.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.050
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:18.130
I am Shareef, the prince of this nation.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.490
Welcome to the Land of Sand. 
We have awaited your arrival.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:24.020
So you are Shareef, then?

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:28.010
I must offer you my gratitude 
for your magnificent gift.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.430
Did it please you?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.170
Yes. The technique it must 
have taken to imbue a tool

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.700
with such magic is impressive indeed.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.890
Thank you.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.110
Emperor Wolfgang...

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:49.110
Did the gift convince you 
of our nation's sincerity?

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.120
<i>He has a very direct, 
straightforward way of speaking.</i>

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.310
<i>I like it.</i>

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:05.880
<i>And it appears this nation has ideas that 
my own would never have come up with.</i>

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.170
Of course.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:12.360
I believe our two nations 
will be good friends.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.410
Thank you very much.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:26.210
<b>Kingdom</b>

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:27.420
I see. So the Empire and the Land of Sand 
are about to forge an alliance?

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:30.910
Yes. The king has already been informed,

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.600
and preparations for war have begun.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:39.390
But he wanted to hear your opinion as 
minister before taking any action.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:43.150
Very well. I will visit the king tomorrow.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:44.530
You may go.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:45.320
Yes, sir.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:50.420
<i>Just what is the Empire planning?</i>

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:54.370
<i>And it was the Land of Sand 
that approached them?</i>

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.550
<i>I can't see what their goal is.</i>

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:04.060
<i>But if I make the wrong judgment here,</i>

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.790
<i>it would insult the king who gave me,</i>

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.320
<i>one who can offer nothing 
but espionage, such a high post.</i>

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.950
<i>Today just happens to be the Day of Satur.</i>

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:20.230
<i>I may be able to acquire some information now,
while the situation is evolving.</i>

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.460
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.710
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.740
Pork cutlet bowl's up.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.470
Okay. I'll take it out.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:33.800
I guess you like all of the 
rice burgers, huh, Alice?

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.800
You gotta save the scallops for last, right?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.310
Yeah! They're so good!

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.100
No, no! The squid should be last!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.270
Kuro-san, two more beers 
in large mugs, please.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.620
Two more? Didn't Artorius-san only want one?

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.320
Oh, I think they're about to...

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.110
Hey! Another draft beer!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:49.990
For me, too!

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.570
Sure, coming right up!

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.200
Welcome!

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.850
The green tea shaved ice 
here is unlike anything else!

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.960
Pork cutlet bowls are so good!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.960
Omelette rice not ready yet?

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:15.030
I'm sorry! Please wait just a bit longer!

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:19.690
Excuse me. A tofu steak and a mixed 
vegetable tempura rice burger, please.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.730
And the usual to take back with us.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.350
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.360
Got it!

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.480
Ah, here it is!

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.730
<i>It's quite crowded again today.</i>

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:33.040
<i>I see the omelette rice lizardman,
 the tofu steak elf,</i>

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.240
<i>the fried seafood dwarf...</i>

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.810
<i>The men from the Land of Mountains
 and Land of Sea...</i>

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.780
<i>The halfling husband and wife...</i>

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.180
<i>I don't imagine I'd learn much about the 
Empire and the Land of Sand from them.</i>

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.250
Thank you for waiting!

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.250
We're a bit crowded at the moment,

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.680
so if you don't mind sharing a table,
 I can show you to one.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:54.960
That's fine.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.030
Thank you! Please follow me.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.920
Pardon me.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.920
<i>The knight of the duchy, 
Heinrich, "Fried Shrimp,"</i>

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:08.520
<i>and the mercenary from the empire, 
Ranija, "Rare Cheesecake."</i>

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.470
<i>I'm fairly sure her origins 
are in the Land of Sand,</i>

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:14.230
<i>which means she might know something.</i>

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:19.280
<i>That's not... Lastina, the demon lord 
who lives in the Empire, is it?!</i>

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.980
<i>So she's also a regular here now?</i>

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.840
<i>But I can't be too hasty in questioning her.</i>

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.330
<i>I've heard she is exceedingly clever.</i>

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.800
Is something wrong?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.790
No, nothing at all.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.290
The usual, please.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.540
Sure! Carbonara, right?

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.180
Coming right up!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.180
I'd like my usual mocha 
chocolate parfait, please.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.260
Waitress, is my fried 
shrimp still not ready?

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:48.440
What about my cheesecake?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.700
I'm so sorry! We're kind of backed up today.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:54.440
Could I trouble you to 
wait just a bit longer?

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:58.240
I see. Well, it is clear that there 
are more customers here than usual.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.150
I suppose that's just how it is.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:02.190
I'm very sorry.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:07.190
We can offer you a complimentary 
quiche while you wait.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.730
Would you like some?

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:09.800
Quiche?

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:13.100
I can't guess what kind of 
dish that is from the name.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.960
What is is made with?

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.570
It is a baked dish of pie crust 
containing cobbler's tubers,

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:21.970
shripe, eggs, and cheese.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:26.220
I'd like one, please. 
Cobbler's tubers are my favorite.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:28.270
I'll have one, too, naturally.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:32.980
I can eat shripe while I wait for 
my fried shrimp? What a laugh!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.740
It uses eggs, eh? Then I'll have one, too.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.620
One for me as well, please.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.240
I wonder what kind of cheese it uses.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.100
Understood. I'll divide it 
up and bring it right away.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.250
Thank you so much, Kuro-san!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.370
They were the master's directions.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:00.470
Besides, you always help me, too.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:01.510
Huh?

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:05.260
Order up. Three types of omelette to go.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.600
Okay. I'll take them out to Gaganpo-san.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.840
You take the quiche. 
I'll take the omelettes.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:15.770
<i>I can converse directly with Gaganpo-san.</i>

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:17.780
Good point!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.580
<i>Is she serious?</i>

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:23.280
<i>Quiche</i>

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:23.280
Thank you for waiting. Here's your quiche.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.930
Ah! So this is quiche?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.160
Let's start on it right away.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.540
Agreed.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.920
Now, what have we here?

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.590
<i>She called this a "pie crust"?</i>

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.900
<i>It supports the densely 
packed fillings very well.</i>

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:45.180
<i>The egg appears to bind all the 
other ingredients together.</i>

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:49.680
<i>The shripe is clearly the star of this dish.</i>

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:51.550
<i>It smells great.</i>

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:54.690
<i>The aroma of cheese piques my appetite.</i>

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:58.790
<i>I didn't expect the cobbler's tubers 
to be spread all over it like this!</i>

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.770
<i>It's very soft and tender overall,</i>

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.850
<i>but the shripe adds just the 
right variation in texture!</i>

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:16.210
<i>The cheese smells so good!</i>

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.780
<i>The cobbler's tubers give it substance.</i>

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.830
<i>It's a simple flavor, seasoned just right.</i>

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:26.220
<i>It bursts when I bite into it, spreading the
 flavor of the ocean in my mouth.</i>

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.300
<i>But it's not just the shripe.</i>

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:31.980
<i>The richness of the eggs and the other 
aromas also vie for my attention!</i>

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:33.730
It's good!

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:33.730
It's delicious!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.400
I am very sorry for the long wait.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.790
It's all right. Thanks for a great meal.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.450
I'll be coming again.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:56.000
Thank you very much. Travel home safely.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.170
I will. Thanks for everything.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.410
Mr. Fried Shrimp...

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:05.010
This shripe is truly exquisite.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:11.010
Yes, but Mr. Carbonara, it is 
the eggs that make this dish.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:16.020
And the strong flavor of the cheese goes 
well with the saltiness of the shrimp.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.990
The cobbler's tubers absorb 
all of the flavors.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:22.030
It's absolutely delicious!

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.410
Adelhe—

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.870
Calm down, Brother!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.620
She's a person of high status, too!

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.480
We must follow the restaurant's customs!

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.920
Y-Yeah... You're right.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.170
Is everything all right?

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.410
Where's Chocolate Parfait!

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:50.180
Did she leave already?!

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:53.480
Um... Is Chocolate Parfait...

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.850
No, she hasn't been here yet today.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:01.290
She hasn't?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:05.690
Brother, everyone is watching. 
Let's sit down for now.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.730
Yeah... Okay.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.660
One coffee float with ice cream.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.690
Make the kaffa extra sweet, please.

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:20.700
And I'll have a soda float with 
melon soda and soft serve.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.910
Your order has been accepted.

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:30.690
<i>Prince Shareef...</i>

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:33.320
<i>He isn't behaving quite like usual.</i>

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:49.610
Master, what do you suppose is 
the matter with Shareef-san?

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:52.080
He is acting differently today, isn't he?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.860
Did something happen between 
him and Adelheid-san?

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:58.720
They always seemed to get along well.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.830
I don't believe there's any problem.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.340
Let's just watch over him.

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:06.160
Watch over him?

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:09.380
Fried shrimp's up. Take it out, would you?

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.930
Oh... Sure!

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.850
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.600
Here's your fried shrimp, your carbonara,

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:19.190
your mocha chocolate parfait, 
and your rare cheesecake.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:21.380
How I've waited for this!

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:30.020
<i>The breading is crispy, 
the shripe is tender,</i>

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.950
<i>and the flavor bursts in 
my mouth with every bite!</i>

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:39.240
<i>This smooth texture along with the mild 
sourness and sweetness just can't be beat!</i>

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.870
<i>I could keep eating this forever!</i>

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.920
<i>The slightly bitter kaffa, 
the sweet chocolate,</i>

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:49.170
<i>and the fluffy cream that 
mellows them both...</i>

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.760
<i>It's so luxurious!</i>

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:57.460
<i>The rich flavor of eggs and the savoriness of 
smoked meat are packed into this sauce!</i>

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:01.020
<i>The way they envelop the 
noodles is truly delicious!</i>

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:08.270
Indeed, fried shrimp is still the best!

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:11.900
I couldn't decide between this 
and the cobbler's tuber dish,

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:15.220
but I was right to choose the mocha 
chocolate parfait again today.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:18.300
Your favorite always comes 
out on top, doesn't it?

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:24.420
Yes, but that quiche earlier was 
a delicious harmony of flavors.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.860
It was.

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:29.320
I never would have thought cheese 
would go so well with shripe.

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:33.170
The pairing of cobbler's tubers 
with eggs was fantastic, too.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.000
Yes, cobbler's tubers are 
the Empire's specialty,

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.430
while shripe is a specialty 
of the Kingdom, isn't it?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:43.670
If we can distribute each of our nations' 
specialties to all other lands,

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:47.360
it would advance the dietary culture 
of our entire world, would it not?

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.900
Ah, that is true!

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.250
You're right.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.940
That sounds lovely!

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:57.530
<i>Perhaps I should propose this to the king.</i>

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:05.090
Brother, if you keep drinking water,
you won't be able to finish your float.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:09.130
Yeah... But I need to do <i>something</i>, 
or I can't calm myself down.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.210
I see.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.630
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:15.310
Here are your coffee float 
and melon soda float.

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.720
<i>Coffee Float</i>

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:22.720
I'm sorry for yelling like that earlier.

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:24.750
Oh, that's all right!

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.480
I'm watching over you!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.830
Huh? Uh, okay...

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.980
Well, enjoy!

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:45.920
<i>It really is delicious.</i>

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.720
<i>The other world's kaffa has a pure flavor,</i>

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:51.160
<i>and the proportion of sourness 
to bitterness is just right.</i>

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.850
<i>The ice cream is nice and cold,</i>

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.920
<i>cooling my body after that 
long walk over the hot sand.</i>

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:04.020
<i>The rich flavor and mild sweetness 
of milk goes well with kaffa.</i>

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.360
<i>Now, I think it's time to sink it in.</i>

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:18.960
<i>The ice cream adds to the kaffa's sweetness</i>

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:21.120
<i>while softening its bitterness.</i>

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.530
<i>It's good this way, too.</i>

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:25.440
<i>You can just eat the ice cream,</i>

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:28.630
<i>just drink the kaffa, or mix them together.</i>

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.780
<i>There are multiple ways to enjoy it.</i>

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:34.300
<i>This is what a coffee float should be!</i>

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:37.460
<i>It looks like he's calmed down a bit.</i>

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:44.270
Brother!

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:45.900
Ow...

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:13.380
Oh, hello there. Is something the matter?

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:14.880
Adelheid!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.380
Yes?

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:18.580
Please marry me.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:29.270
What?!

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:38.030
<i>That's right.</i>

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.780
<i>Eating with others brings 
a feeling of happiness.</i>

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.690
<i>You're the one who taught me that.</i>

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:47.710
<i>And...</i>

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:52.120
<i>Somehow, I feel so happy 
just being here like this.</i>

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:57.260
Yes, I'd be happy to, Prince Shareef!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:00.590
Addy!

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.600
What a happy occasion! 
This calls for a party!

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.680
Everything's on me tonight!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.270
Eat and drink all you want today, everyone!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.850
Another pork cutlet bowl!

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.940
So that's how marriage proposals are done!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.230
How interesting!

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:20.610
Hey, Far, what's "marriage"?

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.740
It means becoming a family.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.750
Oh! That's so nice!

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:25.870
It sure is.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.790
Can I get married, too?

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:29.650
<i>Can</i> you? I'm not sure...

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:31.290
Huh?!

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.800
<i>I can't believe it...</i>

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:42.220
<i>He was trying to curry favor with 
the Empire so he could marry her?</i>

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:46.720
<i>Not bad, Prince of the Land of Sand.</i>

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.320
<i>I must report this to my own nation at once,</i>

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:52.230
<i>and tell them there's no 
need to deploy soldiers.</i>

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.510
<i>I can't just sit here!</i>

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.280
Prince... Shareef...

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.610
Too tight...

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.430
I'm sorry! I was just so...

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.770
Um... When you called me 
"Addy" a moment ago...

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:11.870
That's a special name for me, isn't it?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.180
You didn't like it?

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:17.000
No, it made me happy.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.110
Sharry!

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:19.680
Addy!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:24.440
Watching the two of them 
makes me feel happy, too.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:27.620
I agree. But this was...

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.980
Yes, I did see it coming.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.490
But it seems not everybody did.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:39.020
Master! Shareef-san and Adelheid-san just...

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:42.890
Yeah, I saw. Can't say I expected that.

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:44.280
I know!

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.440
It was so sudden! I couldn't believe it!

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.270
I knew there was no problem.

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:51.340
So that's what you meant 
by "watch over him"!

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:55.610
Jeez! You should've told me 
Shareef-san felt that way!

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.820
It didn't occur to me 
that you hadn't noticed.

00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:03.100
Maybe I'll serve chocolate 
parfaits on the house.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:42.690
<i>Pork Loin Cutlet</i>

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Buffet</i>
